ZCASH BELGIUM

Zcash Belgium is a proposal to build the country's first sustained, physical-first education and adoption network for private digital cash: a permanent hub in Brussels, a rotating circuit of university visits and regional conferences, and a growing group of trained local organizers who can carry the work into their own cities. What follows is our plan for how that comes together, region by region, starting now.

A note on this document. Belgium runs on a lot of different local rhythms - Brussels moves differently than Namur, and a campus in Hasselt keeps a different calendar than one in Mons. So we've written this as a working document rather than a finished one: the campuses, cities, venues, and dates below are our current best plan, and we expect to refine them as real partnerships take shape. Where we've named a specific venue, take it as the target we're pursuing rather than a signed agreement.

One more thing worth flagging up front: most of what follows - the full campus list, the outreach strategy, the flagship events - describes the program at full size, once it's running everywhere. Section 14, the Foundation Roadmap, is the part that says what we're actually doing first, and that's Brussels only, starting with securing funding. Read the rest as the destination, and the roadmap as the first steps toward it.

